NAME
    gcloud alpha number-registry ipam-admin-scopes check-availability - check
        the availability of IPAM admin scopes

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha number-registry ipam-admin-scopes check-availability
        --location=LOCATION --scopes=[SCOPES,...] [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Checks whether the scope of the project is available to be managed.

EXAMPLES
    To check the availability of an organization scope run:

    $ gcloud alpha number-registry ipam-admin-scopes \        check-availability --location=global \
        --scopes organizations/123456789

REQUIRED FLAGS
     Location resource - Parent value for the IpamAdminScopes. This represents
     a Cloud resource. (NOTE) Some attributes are not given arguments in this
     group but can be set in other ways.

     To set the project attribute:
      ◆ provide the argument --location on the command line with a fully
        specified name;
      ◆ provide the argument --project on the command line;
      ◆ set the property core/project.

     This must be specified.

       --location=LOCATION
          ID of the location or fully qualified identifier for the location.

          To set the location attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument --location on the command line.

     --scopes=[SCOPES,...]
        The scopes of the IpamAdminScopes to look for.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --access-token-file, --account,
    --billing-project, --configuration, --flags-file, --flatten, --format,
